# `sh` reads a trailing CR as part of the command, so a shell script checked out with
# CRLF is a broken shell script — `#!/bin/sh\r` is not an interpreter that exists. This
# repository is developed on Windows with core.autocrlf=true, `make release` runs a
# script from that checkout, and `docker build` copies the entrypoint out of the working
# tree rather than out of the index. All three want LF.
*.sh text eol=lf
